[list]
[*]A stand set to Deposit only is no longer somewhere haulers deliver clothing. Outfit stands sit above stockpiles in the storage order, so an empty one had colonists carrying spare apparel to it from across the base, and the slots that filled were the ones its owner needed for their own gear. With Allow removing items held off while a stand is in service, nothing that arrived that way could leave again.
[*]It hit some stands and not others, which is what made it hard to place. A stand that already holds an outfit refuses further deliveries, so among stands set up identically, the deposit-only ones collected clothing and the rest did not. Deposit only is the one mode whose normal state is an empty stand.
[*]You can still put a garment on such a stand yourself: right-click the apparel and target the stand, as before. Only automatic hauling stopped. The sleep change deposits and returns exactly as it did.
[*]A stand that haulers already filled clears itself. At its owner's next change the deposit pushes aside whatever is in the way, and that garment now goes to a stockpile rather than straight back onto the stand.
[/list]
